{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1524786-reality-stalkers-2e-update-help","id":1524786,"title":"Reality Stalkers 2e update - help??","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-30T20:57:25-07:00","id":1524786,"title":"Reality Stalkers 2e update - help??","content":"So,<br /> <br /> My Acanthus player wants to become a Reality Stalker, which is sick, they are a cool legacy. However I am having some problems building them into 2e, so I'm here for some potential insights. Here is what I have so far:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Reality Stalkers<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Sneaks</span><br /> <br /> <br /> Pages 173-176 of The Mysterium and 77 of Nameless and Accursed for Lore<br /> <br /> <br /> Parent Path: Mastigos<br /> Parent Order: The Mysterium<br /> Prerequisites: Space 2, Mind 1, Larceny 2, one of the following additional skills at 2 dots or higher: Athletics, Streetwise Subterfuge, Survival<br /> Initiation: Travel through a crack after having accepted the philosophy and teachings of the legacy.<br /> Ruling Arcana: Space<br /> Yantras: Cracked glass (+1); A Key (+1); <u>Need one more here</u><br /> Oblations: Discovering a secret; Breaking into a building without magic; Traveling long distance without using magic<br /> \u200b<br /> So, let me start out by saying, I <i>hate</i> the attainment in N&amp;A and will not be touching that, no offense to whoever wrote it and I know a lot of people like it, but it doesn't do it for me.<br /> <br /> Anyway, my plan is to make some tweeks to their themes based on how I envision them. The vibe they give in the Mysterium book isn't one of these sneaky people who are using the cracks as spies or thieves, they aren't GotV. Instead I like them as potentially that, but primarily I see them as explorers, going through the fractures of the world to see what is on the other side. Sure, you can use these attainments to steal or to spy, but I enjoy that being secondary to the explorer theme, and my player seemed to be okay with this.<br /> <br /> So, I want to make them Iris mages basically, a legacy of mages that use Space to understand and use <i>all</i> Irises, or at least being able to. A sneak with 0 Death will probably not go through a Iris to the UInderworld, but they <i>should</i> be able to if they want to. Basically, the fractures they see and use is any Iris, I like this idea a lot. The current plan is to use the Space attainments they gain to allow them to see and then interact with Irises, and eventually create their own (this will probably be more limited, you probably <i>will</i> need some Death if you wanna make a fracture to the Underworld, to keep with this example). For the Space attainments I think this is fine, and already have an attainment in mind that will have a double effect, instead of having a secondary arcana avalible, it'll be two Space effects, the ability to notice <i>all</i> Irises, even closed ones, with PMS, and then the ability to learn the key of any Iris they can touch, or could touch if it was physical. After that the attainments will diverge, with Space attainments continuing to mess with Irises, while the optional attainments will become Mind, after all, some Irises take your concious into the Astral, so the Mind optional attainments will grant protection and utility in the Astral, so that the magic can be used there. <br /> <br /> This does leave Death/Underworld and Spirit/Shadow a weak point for them, even though they can access it they can't really do as much there but I don't see a huge problem with that, they are explorers, they will be preping before they go in (hopefully).<br /> <br /> What do you think, does this <i>work</i>? Or does it only sound good in my head and I should get back to the basics before I spend time developing the attainments?<br /> <br /> -TY","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T21:58:02-07:00","id":1524788,"title":"","content":"The 1e book already mentions a tension between the 'theoretical' members and the 'practical' members, so the lore side isn't <i>that</i> much of a change.<br /> <br /> In fact, all their 1e Attainments use Mind as the Optional effects' requirements, so you could translate most of that to 2e. They're all about obfuscation though, having nothing to do with Synesi (Astral Irises), so there's that to consider...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T22:45:04-07:00","id":1524790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1524786-reality-stalkers-2e-update-help?p=1524788#post1524788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 1e book already mentions a tension between the 'theoretical' members and the 'practical' members, so the lore side isn't <i>that</i> much of a change.<br /> <br /> In fact, all their 1e Attainments use Mind as the Optional effects' requirements, so you could translate most of that to 2e. They're all about obfuscation though, having nothing to do with Synesi (Astral Irises), so there's that to consider...</div> </div> </div> </div>I did look over that and it also isn't bad but idk if I like the idea of having attainments designed to hide you from everyone in a group game. Maybe its a lack of expereince thing on my part, but it feels more like a solo play kinda attainment, as opposed to a game with multiple players who you'd also be invisible too (literally invisible or obfuscate levels of invisible, w/e)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T23:15:04-07:00","id":1524791,"title":"","content":"It could be something that allows a party to have a greater stealth focus. Gathering data, hiding secret rooms, hidden compartments and equipment caches. Accessing places they were not supposed to.<br /> <br /> If an Attainment cloaks you, nothing stops you from using it on your cabal members. You could even bargain its use for a boon with those outside the cabal, no need to worry about dispellation and no spell control limit makes for one great bargaining chip.The practical side of the Legacy could be about espionage and thieving. Sure, you will need help getting to the Shadow, but you will keep tabs on that suspicious spurit court like no one else.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T23:17:25-07:00","id":1524792,"title":"","content":"It's nice for doing infiltration work!<br /> <br /> ... Which skirts close to the part of the Reality Stalkers you specifically wanted to avoid, so yeah. You'll have to make your own.<br /> <br /> My rendition (in my sig) had them messing with Irises too with their Attainments' main effects, but not to the extent that you seem to wish for. And the optional effects still had Spirit/Death involved. I'd recommend mining mine for ideas, but the differences are clear...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm. At least from the OP, the idea of Reality Stalkers 'hacking' Irises to use them with Space alone and no other Arcana doesn't seem too alien of a concept. I'll probably put effects like that on the Third and above Attainments though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T03:20:59-07:00","id":1524800,"title":"","content":"Here are some extra Yantras I homebrewed for them a long time ago:<br /> <br /> Reality Stalkers<br /> Succeeding on a L\u0336a\u0336r\u0336c\u0336e\u0336n\u0336y Science or Stealth roll relevant to the spell (+2)<br /> Equipment for geodesic measurements (+1)<br /> Making occult-mathematical calculations (+1, +2 if they take time)<br /> Ritually prepared passageways (+1, +2 if tailored to the spell)\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T09:27:32-07:00","id":1524813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1524786-reality-stalkers-2e-update-help?p=1524792#post1524792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's nice for doing infiltration work!<br /> <br /> ... Which skirts close to the part of the Reality Stalkers you specifically wanted to avoid, so yeah. You'll have to make your own.<br /> <br /> My rendition (in my sig) had them messing with Irises too with their Attainments' main effects, but not to the extent that you seem to wish for. And the optional effects still had Spirit/Death involved. I'd recommend mining mine for ideas, but the differences are clear...</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually seen yours! Moggle recoemnded it and sent it my way when I started talking about these guys yesterday, I was excited when I saw your comment on my post<br /> <br /> And Kaiser makes a good point for me that I didn't consider, hiding the group isn't a bad attainment, might readjust my initial idea, maybe go with Incog Pressence like they did in 1e and just leave the mana cost on it, so it isn't something they are just throwing around but, when they need it on themselves or their entire cabal, its around.<br /> <br /> Much thinking must be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T09:28:35-07:00","id":1524814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1524786-reality-stalkers-2e-update-help?p=1524791#post1524791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If an Attainment cloaks you, nothing stops you from using it on your cabal members. You could even bargain its use for a boon with those outside the cabal, no need to worry about dispellation and no spell control limit makes for one great bargaining chip.The practical side of the Legacy could be about espionage and thieving. Sure, you will need help getting to the Shadow, but you will keep tabs on that suspicious spurit court like no one else.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>THat's valid and does give me an idea, back to the think tank (my job where I obsess over MtAw stuff)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T10:02:48-07:00","id":1524928,"title":"","content":"Well, I decided to let them keep their sneaky attainments, I do think it fits their themes better than using their Mind attainments for astral travel.<br /> <br /> I do still want to not give them a Mind attainment at the first level and hold off until next level which also makes me want to remove Mind as a prerequisite to join, any ideas on what I should replace that with? Not occultation","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T19:41:13-07:00","id":1524954,"title":"","content":"Space is primary, Mind is optional. So you should be able to remove it from the prerequisites. The <i>Piercing Glance</i> merit sounds appropriate (<i>Signs of Sorcery</i> page 26), giving them a way to detect concealed Irises and magically concealed areas.<br /> <br /> I would like to suggest a second option: deviate entirely and make them masters of perception, focusing on Forces as their secondary Arcana. Here is a rough draft of the Attainments:<br /> <br /> <b>Space 1</b><br /> <br /> <i>The Outward &amp; Inward Eye</i>, with Reach assigned to advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Forces 1</b><br /> <br /> <i>Receiver </i>with Reach assigned to advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Space 2</b><br /> <br /> <i>Intrusion Warning</i> (<i>Guardians of the Veil</i> Order book page 198) with Reach assigned to instant use and advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Forces 2</b><br /> <br /> <i>Nightvision </i>with Reach assigned to advanced duration and auto adjusting to extreme stimuli.<br /> <br /> <b>Space 3</b><br /> <br /> <i>Locate Object</i>, with Reach assigned to instant use, sensory range and advanced scale.<br /> <br /> <b>Forces 3</b><br /> <br /> <i>Tune In</i> with Reach assigned to advanced duration and adding [Potency] to rolls to parse through the data (custom Reach option).<br /> <br /> <b>Space 4</b><br /> <br /> <i>Scrying </i>with Reach assigned to instant use, sensory range and advanced duration.<br /> <br /> <b>Forces 4</b><br /> <br /> <i>Zoom In</i> with Reach assigned to advanced duration, seeing for miles and perceiving dust sized particles.<br /> <br /> <b>Space 5</b><br /> <br /> <i>Teleport </i>with Reach assigned to instant use and sensory range.<br /> <br /> <b>Forces 5</b><br /> <br /> <i>Transmission </i>with Reach assigned to instant use, remote range and encrypting a message.<br /> <br /> When examined holistically, this builds up to a very useful toolkit, especially if you give the option to spend a mana for sympathetic range on the ones that are cast at sensory range.<br /> <br /> They are capable of seeing for miles, are aware of minute details that others cannot see, perceive spectrums of sound and energy others can't, can see in the dark, are nearly impossible to surprise, can make custom alarms and can set up a scrying network. They can scout out places before a heist, locate anything quickly, setup warnings against guards, move anything and anyone within their miles wide perception, download or upload data remotely and utilize a much greater sensory range in spellcasting.<br /> <br /> All of that without hiding anything and focusing on the pursuit of information, all in line with the Mysterium's creed. But their methods are under constant suspicion of being too in line with the Panopticon, admonishing them to think carefully how they use their Attainments. But its a small price to pay, because if there is an Iris, they are primed to find it and, once inside, they can examine it in much richer detail than anyone else, instantly contacting any relevant specialists and securely documenting any key details using their Scrying network and mastery of data transmissions.<br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 11-02-2023, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-02T21:07:58-07:00","id":1524955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1524786-reality-stalkers-2e-update-help?p=1524928#post1524928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I decided to let them keep their sneaky attainments, I do think it fits their themes better than using their Mind attainments for astral travel.<br /> <br /> I do still want to not give them a Mind attainment at the first level and hold off until next level which also makes me want to remove Mind as a prerequisite to join, any ideas on what I should replace that with? Not occultation</div> </div> </div> </div>We never needed to make the optional effects' Arcanum an initiation requirement, so you can safely exclude Mind from the prerequisites.<br /> <br /> For the 1st Attainment; maybe something that augments Mind Sight? Like the Eleventh Question's 1st Attainment's optional effect does.<br /> <br /> E.g. If the 1st Attainment's main effect (Space) is something like detecting and analyzing Irises, the optional effect could be something like &quot;The mage may reflexively activate Mind Sight as she studies the Iris via the Attainment, gaining successes equal to Mind dots for piercing concealment via Clash of Wills. Furthermore, she may extend Mind Sight through and beyond the Iris, scanning its immediate vicinity as if she was there.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T16:59:00-07:00","id":1525000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1524786-reality-stalkers-2e-update-help?p=1524955#post1524955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We never needed to make the optional effects' Arcanum an initiation requirement, so you can safely exclude Mind from the prerequisites.<br /> <br /> For the 1st Attainment; maybe something that augments Mind Sight? Like the Eleventh Question's 1st Attainment's optional effect does.<br /> <br /> E.g. If the 1st Attainment's main effect (Space) is something like detecting and analyzing Irises, the optional effect could be something like &quot;The mage may reflexively activate Mind Sight as she studies the Iris via the Attainment, gaining successes equal to Mind dots for piercing concealment via Clash of Wills. Furthermore, she may extend Mind Sight through and beyond the Iris, scanning its immediate vicinity as if she was there.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This was gonna be the first attainment<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment: Noticing the Cracks</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Prerequisites: Initiation</i><br /> The first skill a sneak must learn is to notice the fractures in the fallen world and understand them. This attainment has two functions, the first causes allows for the mages peripheral mage sight to notice all irises, even those that are closed, as if they are an active magical effect, and allows the mages active Space sight to see all irises, open or closed, as effects that fall under the Space arcana. The second power gained from this attainment allows the sneak to learn the key of any iris within touching distance.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-03T18:15:00-07:00","id":1525006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aendrinastor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1524786-reality-stalkers-2e-update-help?p=1525000#post1525000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This was gonna be the first attainment<br /> <br /> <b>First Attainment: Noticing the Cracks</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Prerequisites: Initiation</i><br /> The first skill a sneak must learn is to notice the fractures in the fallen world and understand them. This attainment has two functions, the first causes allows for the mages peripheral mage sight to notice all irises, even those that are closed, as if they are an active magical effect, and allows the mages active Space sight to see all irises, open or closed, as effects that fall under the Space arcana. The second power gained from this attainment allows the sneak to learn the key of any iris within touching distance.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Space Active Sight as-is already detects the presence of Irises. So adding that to Peripheral Sight is a good idea, but this means that you need something else if you want to boost normal Space Sight. How about enabling Space Sight to intuit whether the detected Irises have Keys, and whether the mage himself fulfills those Keys or not at this moment? (So to figure out what the Key of an Iris exactly is, he still needs to study it.)<br /> <br /> Still drawing a blank for what the optional effect could be. If all else fails, you could just accept the asymmetry and leave it empty... assuming that the players agree, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T11:54:05-07:00","id":1525026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1524786-reality-stalkers-2e-update-help?p=1525006#post1525006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Space Active Sight as-is already detects the presence of Irises. So adding that to Peripheral Sight is a good idea, but this means that you need something else if you want to boost normal Space Sight. How about enabling Space Sight to intuit whether the detected Irises have Keys, and whether the mage himself fulfills those Keys or not at this moment? (So to figure out what the Key of an Iris exactly is, he still needs to study it.)<br /> <br /> Still drawing a blank for what the optional effect could be. If all else fails, you could just accept the asymmetry and leave it empty... assuming that the players agree, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>well the first attainment has two functions to it already, a knowing effect (learning the keys of Irises) and an unveiling effect (PMS picking up closed Irises)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26284-aendrinastor","name":"Aendrinastor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26284_6.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"276"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}